### Platform

macOS

### Version

v1.7.12

### Bug Description

Cherry Studio does not support the latest mcp protocol. An error was reported when adding MCP Server：
`Error invoking remote method 'mcp:list-tools': Error: required value must be ["array"] `

<img width="400" height="290" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e5636b3f-da1a-4a6d-8585-36c09d51c728" />

The latest mcp protocol  `tools/list` response schema like this:
```json
{
    "id": 1,
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "result": {
        "tools": [
            {
                "name": "testget",
                "title": "MCP Tool Test GET",
                "description": "This is a test get tool for MCP client",
                "inputSchema": {
                    "additionalProperties": false,
                    "properties": {
                        "name": {
                            "description": "Name of the user making the request",
                            "type": "string"
                        },
                        "traceId": {
                            "description": "Trace ID for tracking the request",
                            "type": "string"
                        }
                    },
                    "required": [
                        "name",
                        "traceId"
                    ],
                    "type": "object"
                },
                "outputSchema": {
                    "additionalProperties": false,
                    "properties": {
                        "data": {
                            "description": "Response code indicating the status of the request",
                            "type": "string"
                        }
                    },
                    "required": [
                        "code"
                    ],
                    "type": "object"
                }
            }
        ]
    }
}
```

After I attempted to set the `properties` attribute of outputSchema to `{}`, the addition was successful！！！😒

### Steps To Reproduce

1. Click on MCP service and configure it
2. Click the switch
3. Wait for a while and this error appears

### Expected Behavior

Should be able to see the list of all tools

### Relevant Log Output

```shell

```

### Additional Context

No response

