### Issue Checklist

- [x] I have searched through the existing issues and did not find a similar report.
- [x] I have provided a short and descriptive title.

### Platform

macOS, Windows

### Version

v1.7.24+

### Bug Description

OpenClaw one-click installation fails because the upstream dependency `@whiskeysockets/baileys` references a git URL dependency `libsignal@git+https://github.com/whiskeysockets/libsignal-node.git`. When running npm install, it needs to call `git ls-remote` to clone this repository, which fails in the following scenarios:

**macOS**: The user has not installed Xcode Command Line Tools. `/usr/bin/git` exists as a shim but cannot actually execute git operations. `checkGitAvailable()` detects that git exists and returns `available: true`, but npm install fails with a git error when running.

**Windows**: The user's git is configured with `url.\"git@github:\".insteadOf`, forcing HTTPS to be converted to SSH protocol, but the user has not configured an SSH Key, resulting in `Permission denied (publickey)`.

### Root Cause Analysis

#### 1. `checkGitAvailable()` detection is too shallow (`src/main/utils/process.ts:498`)

```typescript
export async function checkGitAvailable() {
  const gitPath = await findExecutableInEnv('git')
  return { available: gitPath !== null, path: gitPath }
}
```

Only checks if the git binary exists in PATH, **does not verify if git actually works**. On macOS, `/usr/bin/git` is a shim that exists but is unavailable when Xcode CLT is not installed.

#### 2. Insufficient error handling after installation failure (`OpenClawService.ts:304`)

```typescript
if (stderr.includes('EACCES') || stderr.includes('permission denied')) {
  // Only handles permission errors → sudo retry
} else {
  // Generic failure message, no git-specific guidance
}
```

Only handles EACCES with sudo retry. There is no detection and user guidance for git-related failures (exit code 128, `xcode-select`, `Permission denied (publickey)`, etc.).

### Suggested Fix

#### 1. Enhance `checkGitAvailable()` — Verify git is actually available

```typescript
export async function checkGitAvailable() {
  const gitPath = await findExecutableInEnv('git')
  if (!gitPath) return { available: false, path: null }

  // Actually verify git works (catches macOS Xcode CLT shim)
  try {
    await executeCommand(gitPath, ['--version'], { capture: true, timeout: 5000 })
    return { available: true, path: gitPath }
  } catch {
    return { available: false, path: gitPath }
  }
}
```

#### 2. Add git failure error detection and prompts

In the exit handler of `install()`, add detection for git-related errors:

```typescript
if (stderr.includes('xcode-select') || stderr.includes('No developer tools')) {
  this.sendInstallProgress('Please install Xcode Command Line Tools first: xcode-select --install', 'error')
} else if (stderr.includes('Permission denied (publickey)')) {
  this.sendInstallProgress('Git SSH authentication failed. Please configure SSH Key or run: git config --global url.\"https://github.com/\".insteadOf \"git@github.com:\"', 'error')
}
```

### Error Logs

**macOS:**
```
npm error xcode-select: note: No developer tools were found, requesting install.
npm error command git --no-replace-objects ls-remote ssh://git@github.com/whiskeysockets/libsignal-node.git
```

**Windows:**
```
error code 128
error An unknown git error occurred  
error command git --no-replace-objects ls-remote ssh://git@github.com/whiskeysockets/libsignal-node.git
error git@github.com: Permission denied (publickey).
error fatal: Could not read from remote repository.
```

### Workaround

**macOS:** First run `xcode-select --install` in the terminal to install command line tools, then click install OpenClaw.

**Windows:** Run `git config --global url.\"https://github.com/\".insteadOf \"git@github.com:\"` in the terminal to force git to use HTTPS, then retry the installation.

### Related

- #13333 (sudo PATH issue, PR #13356 exists)
- Upstream dependency: `@whiskeysockets/baileys` → `libsignal@git+https://github.com/whiskeysockets/libsignal-node.git`

